{"id": "171021", "revid": "235382", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=171021", "title": "Nipawin", "text": "Nipawin is a town of 4,400 (2016) in Northern Saskatchewan. This resort community has become a destination for fishing, camping, boating, golfing, hunting and outdoor recreation.\nUnderstand.\nNipawin is located on the shores of Tobin and Codette Lakes along the Saskatchewan River.\nGet in.\nBy car.\nNipawin sits at the junctions of Highway 35 and Highway 55. It is 270 km northeast of Saskatoon by taking Highways 41, 3 and 35.\nBy plane.\nThere is no scheduled air service to Nipawin. The nearest commercial airport in Saskatoon. Nipawin has a small airport 2.4 km south of town."}
{"id": "171023", "revid": "1201546", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=171023", "title": "Right Bank", "text": "Right Bank in the abstract refers to the right side (seen in the direction of flow; so in a river that flows from South to North, the right bank would be to the East) of a river. The term has come to refer to parts of various cities:"}
{"id": "171041", "revid": "235382", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=171041", "title": "Sainte-Marie-aux-Mines", "text": "Sainte-Marie-aux-Mines is a commune in the Haut-Rhin department of Alsace.\nUnderstand.\nAs the name suggests, Sainte-Marie draws its fame from the mines on which it is built, which have been known since Roman antiquity and excavated for precious metals such as antimony."}
{"id": "171049", "revid": "235382", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=171049", "title": "Severodvinsk", "text": "Severodvinsk is a city of just under 200,000 inhabitants in Arkhangelsk Oblast. \nUnderstand.\nThe city is the center of Russian submarine construction. If you're not a Russian citizen, a special permit is required to enter.\nGet in.\nBuses are available from nearby Arkhangelsk, with at least one departure every 15 minutes during the day, journey time is about one hour.\nRZD operates a train from Moscow every second day, taking around 22 hours. There's also several daily commuter train from Arkhangelsk and nearby towns, however the train is slower compared to buses."}
