{"id": "172970", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=172970", "title": "Wainwright", "text": "\"For other places with the same name, see (disambiguation).\"\nWainwright is a town of 6,300 people (2016) in East Central Alberta, Canada.\nUnderstand.\nWainwright is 206 km southeast of Edmonton and 61 km south of Vermilion, in the Battle River Valley. The town of Wainwright is surrounded by the Wainwright Municipal District No. 61 and includes its administrative offices. It is adjacent to CFB Wainwright (Denwood), a Canadian military base, and is a divisional point on the Canadian National Railway main line.\nGet in.\nBy train.\n Train operator:\nBy car.\nWainwright is on Highway 14, 206 km southeast of Edmonton and 69 km west of the Saskatchewan border. It is also accessible via Highway 41, located 61 km south of Vermilion."}
{"id": "172979", "revid": "2441334", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=172979", "title": "Rock Hall", "text": "Rock Hall is a small town on the Eastern Shore of Maryland.\nUnderstand.\nRock Hall is a town of about 1,300 people on the coast of Maryland's scenic Eastern Shore. Despite its small size, the so-called \"Pearl of the Chesapeake\" offers a surprising array of sights and experiences, ranging from concerts and waterfront festivals to fresh Chesapeake bay seafood.\nGet in.\nBy car.\nThe most common way to enter the town is by car via MD 20, which runs from Chestertown to Rockville and other villages on the Eastern Shore.\nBy boat.\nRock Hall is situated right on the water, so travelers with a boat can set it in the town's marinas.\nGet around.\nOn foot, by car, or by bicycle.\nThe town is small enough that you can get around on foot with a bit of patience, though it's still much easier and quicker to use a car or bicycle.\nPublic transportation.\nTrams can transport visitors and residents around town at the price of $1 per person. There are two such trams: one called the Osprey Flyer and another called the Blue Crab Trawler. The service runs from May to November, stopping at various tram stops throughout town, though the schedule may change when there's a holiday like the 4th of July.\nStay safe.\nRock Hall is a very safe town. Though it is hardly an affluent place, everyone knows each other (as they do in most small towns) and crime is quite uncommon."}
{"id": "172996", "revid": "235382", "url": "https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki?curid=172996", "title": "Lindesnes", "text": "Lindesnes is a rural municipality in Agder (South Norway, also called S\u00f8rlandet).\nUnderstand.\nThe main town, Vigeland, has slightly over 1000 inhabitants."}
